# Dictant Quest — development safety

- This is an existing production-like family project. Extend it; do not rewrite it.
- Read `.cursor/skills/dictant-quest/SKILL.md` before UI or product changes.
- Preserve current React + TypeScript + Vite architecture.
- Preserve existing GameStore and cloud compatibility unless the task explicitly requests migration.
- Existing stored user data must remain readable.
- Keep backward compatibility for TodayTask and Settings.
- Never silently reset money, tasks, photos, dictations, settings, or progress.
- Avoid unrelated refactors.
- Do not add dependencies unless they are necessary and explicitly justified.
- Do not redesign screens while implementing logic.
- Phone-first UI only.
- UI language is Russian.
- After every implementation batch run:
  - `npm run typecheck`
  - `npm run build`
- Do not continue to another implementation stage without an explicit user request.
- Before changing more than 4 files, explain why each file needs modification.
- When changing persistence formats, add backwards-compatible decoding/defaults.
- Money changes must be idempotent: one user action must not be credited twice.
- Do not hard-code configurable rewards inside feature logic.
